Generic single-database configuration.
initialisw alembic:
    alembic init alembic
confifure database connection::
    modify env.py --> set SQLAlchemy url (Ensure it matches your FastAPI/SQLAlchemy connection string)
Make model changes
Generate migration script::
    Create a migration that reflects your model changes.
    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "my changes"
    Alembic compares models vs. DB schema, Produces a migration file with ALTER TABLE commands
Apply migration::
    upgrasde database schema:
    alembic upgrade head
    - This will execute migration script
    - adds new colums / constraints and so on
    - Keeps schema version history for rollback if needed

To undo the most recent migrationL
    alembic downgrade -1
Go back to the specific revision ID:
    alembic downgrade <revison_id>
Reset to base:
    alembic downgrade base

Things to consider:
    adding a new colum, do existing rows need a default?
    Adding unique constraint --> do duplicates exist?
    changing types --> will exisitng values fit in the new type
    